  <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p><em>Last updated: November 23, 2026</em></p>

  <p>Danger Apps Inc. built the NameBaby app for iOS and Android. NameBaby is free to use and supported by ads,
      with an optional Premium subscription that removes ads and limits. This SERVICE is provided by
      Danger Apps Inc. and is intended for use as is.</p>
  <p>This page is used to inform visitors regarding our policies with the collection, use, and
      disclosure of Personal Information if anyone decided to use our Service.</p>
  <p>If you choose to use our Service, then you agree to the collection and use of information in relation
      to this policy. The Personal Information that we collect is used for providing and improving the
      Service. We will not use or share your information with anyone except as described
      in this Privacy Policy.</p>
  <p>The terms used in this Privacy Policy have the same meanings as in our
      <a href="/name_baby/terms/">Terms and Conditions</a> unless otherwise defined in this Privacy Policy.</p>

  <h3>Information Collection and Use</h3>
  <p>You can use NameBaby without creating an account. What we handle depends on which features you use.</p>

  <h4>Information stored on your device</h4>
  <p>Unless you sign in, the following stays on your device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The names you like, dislike and add to your short list, your search history and your chat history.</li>
    <li>Your settings: the baby's last name, middle names, how many babies you are expecting, your first name
        (this defaults to “Me”), your filters and your theme.</li>
    <li>An optional “baby's ethnicity” setting. It is used only to choose which preview photos to show you,
        and it defaults to “Prefer not to say”.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Account (optional)</h4>
  <p>You can sign in with your email address. Sign-in is passwordless: we email you a sign-in link. If you sign in,
      we collect your email address and assign you a user ID. Accounts are provided through Google's
      Firebase Authentication. The sign-in email is sent through our email provider, Resend, and we briefly keep
      a hashed (scrambled) form of your email address to limit how many sign-in emails can be requested.</p>

  <h4>Cloud sync</h4>
  <p>Once you are signed in, the following is saved to our cloud database (Google Cloud Firestore) under your
      user ID:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The settings listed above, including the baby's last name, your first name and the “baby's ethnicity” setting.</li>
    <li>Your baby details.</li>
    <li>Your lists of liked, disliked and short-listed names.</li>
    <li>Your email address.</li>
    <li>Whether you have Premium.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="confirm">[CONFIRM: search history and chat history are not in the synced list you gave me, so this
      policy does not say they are synced. Check that is right.]</p>

  <h4>Partner sharing (optional)</h4>
  <p>Two NameBaby users can link their accounts. When you do, a shared record holds each person's first name,
      email address and their liked, disliked and short-listed names. Your partner can see your first name,
      your email address and the names you have liked and short-listed. You can see the same about them.</p>

  <h4>AI chat</h4>
  <p>When you ask our Name bot for suggestions, the text you type, together with your last three chat exchanges,
      is sent to our server at www.namebabyapp.com. Our server passes it to an AI service provider to generate
      the suggestions. The app does not attach your account ID to these requests. Please do not include
      information in a chat that you would not want to share.</p>
  <p class="confirm">[CONFIRM: which AI provider the server uses (the app code suggests Google Gemini), whether
      our server or the provider logs or stores chat text and for how long, and whether the provider may use it
      to improve its own models. This section should name the provider and state the retention once known.]</p>

  <h4>Name details and previews</h4>
  <p>The app requests name details and preview images from our server at www.namebabyapp.com. A request for a
      preview image tells our server which name you are viewing and your “baby's ethnicity” setting. Some name
      photos are fetched from Wikipedia's public API, which is operated by the Wikimedia Foundation. As with any
      internet request, the server that receives a request can see your device's IP address.</p>
  <p class="confirm">[CONFIRM: what the www.namebabyapp.com server logs for these requests (for example IP
      address, name viewed, ethnicity setting) and how long logs are kept.]</p>

  <h4>Advertising</h4>
  <p>If you do not have Premium, the app shows ads provided by Google AdMob. These include banner, native,
      full-screen and rewarded video ads. You can choose to watch a rewarded video ad to unlock extra AI chats
      and name previews. To show and measure ads, Google's advertising software in the app collects device and
      advertising identifiers, your IP address (from which your approximate location can be inferred), your
      interactions with ads, and diagnostic information, and Google uses this information for advertising.
      Premium subscribers are not shown ads. See “Advertising and Tracking Choices” below for how to
      control this.</p>

  <h4>Analytics</h4>
  <p>We use Google Analytics for Firebase to understand how the app is used. It records app usage events such as:
      a subscription screen being viewed (and from where), a purchase being started or completed, a free limit
      being reached, a rewarded ad being offered or completed, a chat being sent, a name preview being opened,
      and a partner invite being created or accepted. The text of your chats and the names you like are
      <strong>not</strong> sent to analytics. Firebase also collects an app instance ID and general device
      information.</p>
  <p class="confirm">[CONFIRM: Google's documentation says the Analytics SDK also derives general location from
      a masked IP address and, on Android, collects the advertising ID by default. If you have not disabled
      these, add them here. Also confirm you do not set the Firebase user ID on analytics events.]</p>

  <h4>Purchases</h4>
  <p>Premium subscriptions are purchased through Apple's App Store or Google Play. Payment is handled entirely by
      Apple or Google. We never see your payment details. We store only whether you have Premium.</p>

  <h4>Permissions we do not request</h4>
  <p>NameBaby does not request access to your location, contacts, camera, microphone or photos.</p>

  <h3>How We Use Information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the Service: showing names and previews, generating AI suggestions, keeping your lists,
        signing you in, syncing across your devices, and sharing with your partner when you choose to.</li>
    <li>To show ads to users who do not have Premium, and to unlock rewards when you watch a rewarded ad.</li>
    <li>To understand how the app is used so that we can improve it.</li>
    <li>To prevent abuse, such as limiting how many sign-in emails can be requested.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your account information, your lists or your chats.
