  <h3>Advertising and Tracking Choices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>iOS tracking prompt.</strong> On iOS the app can show Apple's tracking permission prompt. Your
        device's advertising identifier is only available to the app if you allow tracking. You can change your
        choice at any time in your device's Settings under Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Tracking.</li>
    <li><strong>Ad Privacy Choices.</strong> In the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, you are shown
        Google's consent form before ads are loaded. You can change your choice later using the
        “Ad Privacy Choices” button in the app's Settings screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Device ad settings.</strong> On Android you can reset or delete your advertising ID in your
        device's Settings (under Google &gt; Ads, or Privacy &gt; Ads, depending on your device). You can also
        manage ad personalization for your Google account at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank">adssettings.google.com</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Premium.</strong> Premium subscribers are not shown ads.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To learn how Google uses information from apps that use its services, see
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</p>

